+Expo handles signing and installation. Expo Go cannot run this app because WebRTC and Rive need a native build.
 
 ## Development
 
 ```sh
 npm run check
-npm run format
 ```
 
-The screen is in `src/screens/live-screen.tsx`. Native controls and Persona renderers are in `src/components`. Call lifecycle and transports are in `src/live`; session configuration and tools are in `src/server`. See [tools](docs/tools.md) to add your own.
-
-Voices are fixed for each call. Persona choices can change at any time. Both choices are saved locally. Calls end after ten minutes; this does not enforce an account spending limit.
-
-See [dependency notes](docs/dependencies.md) for the Xcode workaround and an upstream advisory.
+The call is in `src/call`: one `Call` model (`call.ts`), the session's owner at the app's root (`use-call.tsx`) and the call screen and its parts. Native controls and Persona renderers are in `src/components`, and the session and transport in `src/live`, along with the call's Live Activity (`call-activity.tsx`, built with `expo-widgets`). Its orb stills are rendered from the Persona files by `npm run activity-orbs`. See [dependency notes](docs/dependencies.md) for the Xcode workaround.
 
-MIT. Persona assets retain their [upstream license and attribution](src/components/persona/assets/README.md).
